{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-aaac3e82-32fd-4b94-9be2-16f885001ee9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8358b497cbdf50d8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-d0zyu10e/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for exactly the\nmodels the validation campaign clears, turning the go/no-go scope into a\nshippable platform capability. It extends the existing vLLM runtime\nproductization path (which today ships only CUDA builds) with a ROCm image\nbuild and the corresponding serving runtime definition, so RHOAI can serve\nthe cleared models on AMD Instinct accelerators.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a ROCm build variant of the vLLM serving runtime image to the existing\n  midstream build and release process, based on the upstream ROCm support\n  already published by vLLM.\n- Define the serving runtime resource (ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime)\n  that makes the ROCm runtime available for InferenceServices, scoped to the\n  model list cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Verify end-to-end serving of cleared models on AMD Instinct nodes through\n  the standard KServe InferenceService path.\n- Record the support scope: the runtime is supported for exactly the cleared\n  model list on the validated AMD hardware.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the model list cleared by the validation campaign, when the ROCm\n  runtime image is built, then the build completes green in the existing\n  Konflux build pipeline.\n- Given the built image, when the serving runtime resource is applied, then\n  the ROCm runtime is selectable for InferenceServices platform-wide.\n- Given the productized runtime, when an InferenceService serving a cleared\n  model runs on AMD Instinct nodes, then inference requests succeed\n  end-to-end through the standard serving path.\n- Given the productization, when the support scope is stated, then it covers\n  exactly the models cleared by the campaign and the validated AMD hardware.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities; base-image availability may not align with platform release\n  trains. Tiered delivery: the validation campaign and training-side work\n  deliver value independently of this epic's timing.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — full coverage: a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is\n  productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39811,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a6a655ed610a647","agent_id":"a87fa06e82bd33954","session_id":"9503e158-5f16-4bd9-b154-1147d771dd9b","uuid":"2dd919df-de74-43d7-900e-9d10ba9dcd6f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:34:15.525Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
