{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-82daaf4a-741e-4416-82ae-53b841e224a6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad28c9ce4f681833","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-d0zyu10e/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling and PyTorch ROCm training support\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm a supported capability: single- and\nmulti-GPU PyTorch jobs running on AMD Instinct accelerators are admitted\nthrough Kueue with correct amd.com/gpu quota handling. It extends the\nexisting queueing and quota configuration (which today handles NVIDIA GPUs)\nto the AMD resource name and validates the full training path end to end.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configure Kueue quota handling for the amd.com/gpu resource name\n  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors) so jobs requesting AMD GPUs are\n  admitted with correct quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang) semantics\n  for multi-GPU topologies.\n- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs on ROCm hardware,\n  submitted as PyTorchJobs and admitted through Kueue (the Training Operator\n  requires no code change; this confirms it keeps working on AMD nodes).\n- Document the validated job shapes (single- and multi-GPU) and any driver\n  prerequisites discovered, as input to the platform documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a ClusterQueue configured for amd.com/gpu, when a PyTorchJob\n  requesting AMD GPUs is submitted, then it is admitted with correct quota\n  accounting against the amd.com/gpu resource.\n- Given a multi-GPU PyTorchJob on ROCm, when it is admitted, then it receives\n  its full GPU allocation as an all-or-nothing admission (no partial\n  topologies start).\n- Given single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs using ROCm images,\n  when they run on AMD Instinct nodes after Kueue admission, then the\n  training jobs complete successfully (Training Operator keep-working\n  validation).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** — full coverage: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for\n  single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota\n  handling.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40484,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a6a655ed610a647","agent_id":"a87fa06e82bd33954","session_id":"9503e158-5f16-4bd9-b154-1147d771dd9b","uuid":"c3d92fd9-05d5-4d16-baf3-92118be20784","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:34:22.989Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
