{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83e131cd5bd39514","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: # AMD Instinct ROCm vLLM serving validation campaign\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: ## Description\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: This investigation resolves the strategy's core unknown: whether vLLM serving\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: on AMD Instinct accelerators via ROCm achieves functional and performance\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: parity with the productized CUDA builds for the platform's supported model\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware and\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: produces the per-model go/no-go scope that determines what gets productized.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: Until this question is answered, the productization work cannot be scoped.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: ## Scope\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Stand up a validation environment on dedicated AMD Instinct nodes with the\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   upstream ROCm runtime images and vLLM ROCm builds as published upstream.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Execute functional validation of vLLM serving for every model in the\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   supported model set, recording pass/fail per model.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Execute performance validation (serving throughput and latency) per model\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   against the CUDA baseline, using the platform's standard benchmark\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   methodology.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Validate that vLLM ROCm runtimes deploy and serve through the standard\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   KServe InferenceService path on AMD Instinct nodes (KServe requires no code\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   change; this confirms it keeps working).\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Produce the campaign report: per-model functional results, performance\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   parity data, and a per-model go/no-go recommendation constituting the\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   productization scope.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: ## Acceptance Criteria\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Given the supported model set, when each model is served with vLLM on ROCm\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   on AMD Instinct hardware, then a functional pass/fail result is recorded\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   for every model in the set.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Given the functional results, when serving throughput and latency are\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   measured, then performance parity data relative to the CUDA baseline is\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   recorded per model.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Given vLLM ROCm runtimes, when they are deployed as KServe\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   InferenceServices on AMD Instinct nodes, then deployment and inference\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   succeed through the standard serving path (KServe keep-working validation).\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Given the collected data, when the campaign concludes, then a published\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   report states a go/no-go recommendation per model, defining the\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   productization scope for the serving runtime.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: ## Risks\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - Hardware access: dedicated AMD Instinct nodes must be secured via\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   procurement or a partner lab; this availability precondition is\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   externally controlled and gates campaign execution, not campaign design.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: ## HLR Traceability\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md: - **HLR-1 (P0)** — full coverage: the campaign on physical AMD Instinct\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   hardware establishes the functional and performance parity data for vLLM\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   serving of the supported model set and produces the go/no-go scope for\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md:   productization.\nBODY CROSS-REF FOUND in artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: # Productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: ## Description\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: \nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: This epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for exactly the\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: models the validation campaign clears, turning the go/no-go scope into a\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: shippable platform capability. It extends the existing vLLM runtime\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md: productization path (which today ships only CUDA builds) with a RO