{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ee64697c439c2a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct ROCm vLLM serving validation campaign\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct ROCm vLLM serving validation campaign\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's core unknown: whether vLLM serving\n30\ton AMD Instinct accelerators via ROCm achieves functional and performance\n31\tparity with the productized CUDA builds for the platform's supported model\n32\tset. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware and\n33\tproduces the per-model go/no-go scope that determines what gets productized.\n34\tUntil this question is answered, the productization work cannot be scoped.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Stand up a validation environment on dedicated AMD Instinct nodes with the\n39\t  upstream ROCm runtime images and vLLM ROCm builds as published upstream.\n40\t- Execute functional validation of vLLM serving for every model in the\n41\t  supported model set, recording pass/fail per model.\n42\t- Execute performance validation (serving throughput and latency) per model\n43\t  against the CUDA baseline, using the platform's standard benchmark\n44\t  methodology.\n45\t- Validate that vLLM ROCm runtimes deploy and serve through the standard\n46\t  KServe InferenceService path on AMD Instinct nodes (KServe requires no code\n47\t  change; this confirms it keeps working).\n48\t- Produce the campaign report: per-model functional results, performance\n49\t  parity data, and a per-model go/no-go recommendation constituting the\n50\t  productization scope.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given the supported model set, when each model is served with vLLM on ROCm\n55\t  on AMD Instinct hardware, then a functional pass/fail result is recorded\n56\t  for every model in the set.\n57\t- Given the functional results, when serving throughput and latency are\n58\t  measured, then performance parity data relative to the CUDA baseline is\n59\t  recorded per model.\n60\t- Given vLLM ROCm runtimes, when they are deployed as KServe\n61\t  InferenceServices on AMD Instinct nodes, then deployment and inference\n62\t  succeed through the standard serving path (KServe keep-working validation).\n63\t- Given the collected data, when the campaign concludes, then a published\n64\t  report states a go/no-go recommendation per model, defining the\n65\t  productization scope for the serving runtime.\n66\t\n67\t## Risks\n68\t\n69\t- Hardware access: dedicated AMD Instinct nodes must be secured via\n70\t  procurement or a partner lab; this availability precondition is\n71\t  externally controlled and gates campaign execution, not campaign design.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — full coverage: the campaign on physical AMD Instinct\n76\t  hardware establishes the functional and performance parity data for vLLM\n77\t  serving of the supported model set and produces the go/no-go scope for\n78\t  productization.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974e7d2825fb6355","agent_id":"a8a800091a5010188","session_id":"9503e158-5f16-4bd9-b154-1147d771dd9b","uuid":"a6e3ae75-1206-483d-b862-866342188f88","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:36:37.358Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ee64697c439c2a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
