{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e01547fb8688ee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the campaign clears a reduced model set, productize only those\n15\t    models; if no model clears parity, remove this epic and feed the gap analysis\n16\t    into an upstream remediation plan with AMD.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for exactly the\n39\tmodels the validation campaign clears, turning the go/no-go scope into a\n40\tshippable platform capability. It extends the existing vLLM runtime\n41\tproductization path (which today ships only CUDA builds) with a ROCm image\n42\tbuild and the corresponding serving runtime definition, so RHOAI can serve\n43\tthe cleared models on AMD Instinct accelerators.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Add a ROCm build variant of the vLLM serving runtime image to the existing\n48\t  midstream build and release process, based on the upstream ROCm support\n49\t  already published by vLLM.\n50\t- Define the serving runtime resource (ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime)\n51\t  that makes the ROCm runtime available for InferenceServices, scoped to the\n52\t  model list cleared by the validation campaign.\n53\t- Verify end-to-end serving of cleared models on AMD Instinct nodes through\n54\t  the standard KServe InferenceService path.\n55\t- Record the support scope: the runtime is supported for exactly the cleared\n56\t  model list on the validated AMD hardware.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given the model list cleared by the validation campaign, when the ROCm\n61\t  runtime image is built, then the build completes green in the existing\n62\t  Konflux build pipeline.\n63\t- Given the built image, when the serving runtime resource is applied, then\n64\t  the ROCm runtime is selectable for InferenceServices platform-wide.\n65\t- Given the productized runtime, when an InferenceService serving a cleared\n66\t  model runs on AMD Instinct nodes, then inference requests succeed\n67\t  end-to-end through the standard serving path.\n68\t- Given the productization, when the support scope is stated, then it covers\n69\t  exactly the models cleared by the campaign and the validated AMD hardware.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks\n72\t\n73\t- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n74\t  communities; base-image availability may not align with platform release\n75\t  trains. Tiered delivery: the validation campaign and training-side work\n76\t  deliver value independently of this epic's timing.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — full coverage: a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is\n81\t  productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974e7d2825fb6355","agent_id":"a8a800091a5010188","session_id":"9503e158-5f16-4bd9-b154-1147d771dd9b","uuid":"b04f7047-b205-4538-83e0-88a177e98fb6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:36:37.965Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e01547fb8688ee","permission_decision":{"decision":