{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a330b45fd9b13922","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling and PyTorch ROCm training support\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling and PyTorch ROCm training support\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes PyTorch training on ROCm a supported capability: single- and\n34\tmulti-GPU PyTorch jobs running on AMD Instinct accelerators are admitted\n35\tthrough Kueue with correct amd.com/gpu quota handling. It extends the\n36\texisting queueing and quota configuration (which today handles NVIDIA GPUs)\n37\tto the AMD resource name and validates the full training path end to end.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Configure Kueue quota handling for the amd.com/gpu resource name\n42\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue resource flavors) so jobs requesting AMD GPUs are\n43\t  admitted with correct quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang) semantics\n44\t  for multi-GPU topologies.\n45\t- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs on ROCm hardware,\n46\t  submitted as PyTorchJobs and admitted through Kueue (the Training Operator\n47\t  requires no code change; this confirms it keeps working on AMD nodes).\n48\t- Document the validated job shapes (single- and multi-GPU) and any driver\n49\t  prerequisites discovered, as input to the platform documentation.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a ClusterQueue configured for amd.com/gpu, when a PyTorchJob\n54\t  requesting AMD GPUs is submitted, then it is admitted with correct quota\n55\t  accounting against the amd.com/gpu resource.\n56\t- Given a multi-GPU PyTorchJob on ROCm, when it is admitted, then it receives\n57\t  its full GPU allocation as an all-or-nothing admission (no partial\n58\t  topologies start).\n59\t- Given single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs using ROCm images,\n60\t  when they run on AMD Instinct nodes after Kueue admission, then the\n61\t  training jobs complete successfully (Training Operator keep-working\n62\t  validation).\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — full coverage: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for\n67\t  single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota\n68\t  handling.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974e7d2825fb6355","agent_id":"a8a800091a5010188","session_id":"9503e158-5f16-4bd9-b154-1147d771dd9b","uuid":"c5430786-bc80-4e2f-b44b-5870c3de88be","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:36:39.973Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a330b45fd9b13922","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
